  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Supprocom/MathBlocks",
  "published": "2026-11-08T09:28:31.423Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Patch release. Results are bit-identical to 0.6.0 on CoreCLR and CUDA, except one fix: sequence.convolution@1 with exactly one empty operand is now invalid on CoreCLR, as it already was on CUDA. Faster on CoreCLR: elementwise forms, especially minimum and maximum; vector arithmetic and finiteness checks; and window.path.total-variation@1. Faster on CUDA: Spearman rank counts, Poisson CDF, distance correlation, Whitney and McShane extensions, dynamic time warping, and convolution. Adopt 0.6.1 at a run boundary: the CUDA device source, the operation table, the value codec implementation, and the device ABI fingerprint pins differ from 0.6.0, so a consumer that compares contract pins cannot resume or replay runs recorded on 0.6.0. The value codec schema and the causality pins are unchanged. CUDA execution uses the installed NVIDIA driver and CUDA Toolkit 12.0 or later; the package ships no native binaries.",
